<item>
            <title>[PARQUET-1644] Clean up some benchmark code and docs.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/PARQUET-1644</link>
                <project id="12315521" key="PARQUET">Parquet</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Strictly following the instructions on the &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/parquet-mr/tree/fcc5d1a5a669570de3daeafd3f3b7788aa618536/parquet-benchmarks&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;parquet-benchmarks&lt;/a&gt; module doesn&apos;t give meaningful results.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It appears some new benchmarks enter into conflict with the globs specified for others, not all benchmarks are run, and some iterations of write benchmarks aren&apos;t evalulated due to unexpected &quot;file already exists ...&quot; fail-fast returns in the data generator.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This should be cleaned up to encourage using and implementing benchmarks on Parquet code.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
